    {
      "id": "chapter-2",
      "type": "heading",
      "headingLevel": 2,
      "text": "Titus 2",
      "metadata": {
        "translation": "KJV",
        "bookId": "titus",
        "chapter": 2,
        "blockRole": "chapter_heading"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-2-1",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "But speak thou the things which become sound doctrine:",
      "metadata": {
        "translation": "KJV",
        "bookId": "titus",
        "book": "Titus",
        "bookOrder": 56,
        "chapter": 2,
        "verse": 1,
        "reference": "Titus 2:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:titus:2:1",
        "verseId": "kjv-titus-2-1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-2-2",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "That the aged men be sober, grave, temperate, sound in faith, in charity, in patience.",
      "metadata": {
        "translation": "KJV",
        "bookId": "titus",
        "book": "Titus",
        "bookOrder": 56,
        "chapter": 2,
        "verse": 2,
        "reference": "Titus 2:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:titus:2:2",
        "verseId": "kjv-titus-2-2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-2-3",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "The aged women likewise, that they be in behaviour as becometh holiness, not false accusers, not given to much wine, teachers of good things;",
      "metadata": {
        "translation": "KJV",
        "bookId": "titus",
        "book": "Titus",
        "bookOrder": 56,
        "chapter": 2,
        "verse": 3,
        "reference": "Titus 2:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:titus:2:3",
        "verseId": "kjv-titus-2-3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-2-4",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "That they may teach the young women to be sober, to love their husbands, to love their children,",
      "metadata": {
        "translation": "KJV",
        "bookId": "titus",
        "book": "Titus",
        "bookOrder": 56,
        "chapter": 2,
        "verse": 4,
        "reference": "Titus 2:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:titus:2:4",
        "verseId": "kjv-titus-2-4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-2-5",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "To be discreet, chaste, keepers at home, good, obedient to their own husbands, that the word of God be not blasphemed.",
      "metadata": {
        "translation": "KJV",
        "bookId": "titus",
        "book": "Titus",
        "bookOrder": 56,
        "chapter": 2,
        "verse": 5,
        "reference": "Titus 2:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:titus:2:5",
        "verseId": "kjv-titus-2-5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-2-6",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "Young men likewise exhort to be sober minded.",
      "metadata": {
        "translation": "KJV",
        "bookId": "titus",
        "book": "Titus",
        "bookOrder": 56,
        "chapter": 2,
        "verse": 6,
        "reference": "Titus 2:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:titus:2:6",
        "verseId": "kjv-titus-2-6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-2-7",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "In all things shewing thyself a pattern of good works: in doctrine shewing uncorruptness, gravity, sincerity,",
      "metadata": {
        "translation": "KJV",
        "bookId": "titus",
        "book": "Titus",
        "bookOrder": 56,
        "chapter": 2,
        "verse": 7,
        "reference": "Titus 2:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:titus:2:7",
        "verseId": "kjv-titus-2-7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-2-8",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "Sound speech, that cannot be condemned; that he that is of the contrary part may be ashamed, having no evil thing to say of you.",
      "metadata": {
        "translation": "KJV",
        "bookId": "titus",
        "book": "Titus",
        "bookOrder": 56,
        "chapter": 2,
        "verse": 8,
        "reference": "Titus 2:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:titus:2:8",
        "verseId": "kjv-titus-2-8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-2-9",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "Exhort servants to be obedient unto their own masters, and to please them well in all things; not answering again;",
      "metadata": {
        "translation": "KJV",
        "bookId": "titus",
        "book": "Titus",
        "bookOrder": 56,
        "chapter": 2,
        "verse": 9,
        "reference": "Titus 2:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:titus:2:9",
        "verseId": "kjv-titus-2-9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-2-10",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "Not purloining, but shewing all good fidelity; that they may adorn the doctrine of God our Saviour in all things.",
      "metadata": {
        "translation": "KJV",
        "bookId": "titus",
        "book": "Titus",
        "bookOrder": 56,
        "chapter": 2,
        "verse": 10,
        "reference": "Titus 2:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:titus:2:10",
        "verseId": "kjv-titus-2-10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-2-11",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "For the grace of God that bringeth salvation hath appeared to all men,",
      "metadata": {
        "translation": "KJV",
        "bookId": "titus",
        "book": "Titus",
        "bookOrder": 56,
        "chapter": 2,
        "verse": 11,
        "reference": "Titus 2:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:titus:2:11",
        "verseId": "kjv-titus-2-11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-2-12",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "Teaching us that, denying ungodliness and worldly lusts, we should live soberly, righteously, and godly, in this present world;",
      "metadata": {
        "translation": "KJV",
        "bookId": "titus",
        "book": "Titus",
        "bookOrder": 56,
        "chapter": 2,
        "verse": 12,
        "reference": "Titus 2:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:titus:2:12",
        "verseId": "kjv-titus-2-12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-2-13",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "Looking for that blessed hope, and the glorious appearing of the great God and our Saviour Jesus Christ;",
      "metadata": {
        "translation": "KJV",
        "bookId": "titus",
        "book": "Titus",
        "bookOrder": 56,
        "chapter": 2,
        "verse": 13,
        "reference": "Titus 2:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:titus:2:13",
        "verseId": "kjv-titus-2-13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-2-14",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "Who gave himself for us, that he might redeem us from all iniquity, and purify unto himself a peculiar people, zealous of good works.",
      "metadata": {
        "translation": "KJV",
        "bookId": "titus",
        "book": "Titus",
        "bookOrder": 56,
        "chapter": 2,
        "verse": 14,
        "reference": "Titus 2:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:titus:2:14",
        "verseId": "kjv-titus-2-14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-2-15",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "These things speak, and exhort, and rebuke with all authority. Let no man despise thee.",
      "metadata": {
        "translation": "KJV",
        "bookId": "titus",
        "book": "Titus",
        "bookOrder": 56,
        "chapter": 2,
        "verse": 15,
        "reference": "Titus 2:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:titus:2:15",
        "verseId": "kjv-titus-2-15"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "chapter-3",
      "type": "heading",
      "headingLevel": 2,
      "text": "Titus 3",
      "metadata": {
        "translation": "KJV",
        "bookId": "titus",
        "chapter": 3,
        "blockRole": "chapter_heading"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-3-1",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "Put them in mind to be subject to principalities and powers, to obey magistrates, to be ready to every good work,",
      "metadata": {
        "translation": "KJV",
        "bookId": "titus",
        "book": "Titus",
        "bookOrder": 56,
        "chapter": 3,
        "verse": 1,
        "reference": "Titus 3:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:titus:3:1",
        "verseId": "kjv-titus-3-1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-3-2",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "To speak evil of no man, to be no brawlers, but gentle, shewing all meekness unto all men.",
      "metadata": {
        "translation": "KJV",
        "bookId": "titus",
        "book": "Titus",
        "bookOrder": 56,
        "chapter": 3,
        "verse": 2,
        "reference": "Titus 3:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:titus:3:2",
        "verseId": "kjv-titus-3-2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-3-3",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "For we ourselves also were sometimes foolish, disobedient, deceived, serving divers lusts and pleasures, living in malice and envy, hateful, and hating one another.",
      "metadata": {
        "translation": "KJV",
        "bookId": "titus",
        "book": "Titus",
        "bookOrder": 56,
        "chapter": 3,
        "verse": 3,
        "reference": "Titus 3:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:titus:3:3",
        "verseId": "kjv-titus-3-3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-3-4",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "But after that the kindness and love of God our Saviour toward man appeared,",
      "metadata": {
        "translation": "KJV",
        "bookId": "titus",
        "book": "Titus",
        "bookOrder": 56,
        "chapter": 3,
        "verse": 4,
        "reference": "Titus 3:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:titus:3:4",
        "verseId": "kjv-titus-3-4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-3-5",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "Not by works of righteousness which we have done, but according to his mercy he saved us, by the washing of regeneration, and renewing of the Holy Ghost;",
      "metadata": {
        "translation": "KJV",
        "bookId": "titus",
        "book": "Titus",
        "bookOrder": 56,
        "chapter": 3,
        "verse": 5,
        "reference": "Titus 3:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:titus:3:5",
        "verseId": "kjv-titus-3-5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-3-6",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "Which he shed on us abundantly through Jesus Christ our Saviour;",
      "metadata": {
        "translation": "KJV",
        "bookId": "titus",
        "book": "Titus",
        "bookOrder": 56,
        "chapter": 3,
        "verse": 6,
        "reference": "Titus 3:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:titus:3:6",
        "verseId": "kjv-titus-3-6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-3-7",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "That being justified by his grace, we should be made heirs according to the hope of eternal life.",
      "metadata": {
        "translation": "KJV",
        "bookId": "titus",
        "book": "Titus",
        "bookOrder": 56,
        "chapter": 3,
        "verse": 7,
        "reference": "Titus 3:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:titus:3:7",
        "verseId": "kjv-titus-3-7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-3-8",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "This is a faithful saying, and these things I will that thou affirm constantly, that they which have believed in God might be careful to maintain good works. These things are good and profitable unto men.",
      "metadata": {
        "translation": "KJV",
        "bookId": "titus",
        "book": "Titus",
        "bookOrder": 56,
        "chapter": 3,
        "verse": 8,
        "reference": "Titus 3:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:titus:3:8",
        "verseId": "kjv-titus-3-8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-3-9",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "But avoid foolish questions, and genealogies, and contentions, and strivings about the law; for they are unprofitable and vain.",
      "metadata": {
        "translation": "KJV",
        "bookId": "titus",
        "book": "Titus",
        "bookOrder": 56,
        "chapter": 3,
        "verse": 9,
        "reference": "Titus 3:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:titus:3:9",
        "verseId": "kjv-titus-3-9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-3-10",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "A man that is an heretick after the first and second admonition reject;",
      "metadata": {
        "translation": "KJV",
        "bookId": "titus",
        "book": "Titus",
        "bookOrder": 56,
        "chapter": 3,
        "verse": 10,
        "reference": "Titus 3:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:titus:3:10",
        "verseId": "kjv-titus-3-10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-3-11",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "Knowing that he that is such is subverted, and sinneth, being condemned of himself.",
      "metadata": {
        "translation": "KJV",
        "bookId": "titus",
        "book": "Titus",
        "bookOrder": 56,
        "chapter": 3,
        "verse": 11,
        "reference": "Titus 3:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:titus:3:11",
        "verseId": "kjv-titus-3-11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-3-12",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "When I shall send Artemas unto thee, or Tychicus, be diligent to come unto me to Nicopolis: for I have determined there to winter.",
      "metadata": {
        "translation": "KJV",
        "bookId": "titus",
        "book": "Titus",
        "bookOrder": 56,
        "chapter": 3,
        "verse": 12,
        "reference": "Titus 3:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:titus:3:12",
        "verseId": "kjv-titus-3-12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-3-13",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "Bring Zenas the lawyer and Apollos on their journey diligently, that nothing be wanting unto them.",
      "metadata": {
        "translation": "KJV",
        "bookId": "titus",
        "book": "Titus",
        "bookOrder": 56,
        "chapter": 3,
        "verse": 13,
        "reference": "Titus 3:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:titus:3:13",
        "verseId": "kjv-titus-3-13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-3-14",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "And let ours also learn to maintain good works for necessary uses, that they be not unfruitful.",
      "metadata": {
        "translation": "KJV",
        "bookId": "titus",
        "book": "Titus",
        "bookOrder": 56,
        "chapter": 3,
        "verse": 14,
        "reference": "Titus 3:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:titus:3:14",
        "verseId": "kjv-titus-3-14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-3-15",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "All that are with me salute thee. Greet them that love us in the faith. Grace be with you all. Amen.",
      "metadata": {
        "translation": "KJV",
        "bookId": "titus",
        "book": "Titus",
        "bookOrder": 56,
        "chapter": 3,
        "verse": 15,
        "reference": "Titus 3:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:titus:3:15",
        "verseId": "kjv-titus-3-15"
      }
    }
  ],
